INT. COLONY SHIP "MARGINALIA" - BRIDGE - SHIP'S NIGHT

A dim, circular room. Banks of screens. One wall is a viewport onto a vast gas giant, its bands glowing amber.

CAPTAIN YUSRA, fifties, a gray crop, in a worn command jacket, stands at the center console. ENGINEER BOLT, forties, grease up to her elbows, leans over a panel of exposed wiring. DR. SAKURA, thirties, the ship's physician, sits cross-legged on the deck with a medkit. PILOT MATEO, thirties, in the helm chair, scowls at a blinking display. CADET NILS, nineteen, at the comms station, still wearing a training badge.

Alarm klaxons, soft and rhythmic.

YUSRA
Report. All stations.

BOLT
Fuel line's leaking. I can patch it, Captain, but not for long.

MATEO
We're drifting toward the giant's gravity well. Eight hours.

NILS
Captain, I'm getting a signal. It's not ours.

YUSRA
Nils, put it through.

NILS
It's encrypted.

BOLT
Then decrypt it.

NILS
I'm a cadet!

SAKURA
(quietly)
Nils, breathe.

MATEO
Yusra, if we burn the reserve we can slingshot. Maybe.

YUSRA
Maybe is not a plan.

BOLT
Maybe is all I've got.

SAKURA
Captain, the passengers are asking for updates.

YUSRA
Tell them we have a minor delay.

SAKURA
They won't believe that.

YUSRA
Then tell them a major one, with confidence.

NILS
The signal is a voice. A woman's voice. She's saying coordinates.

MATEO
Where?

NILS
Sector twelve. Near the ring debris.

BOLT
There's a station in sector twelve. Old. Abandoned.

YUSRA
Is it abandoned?

NILS
It's broadcasting.

MATEO
Captain, it could be a trap.

YUSRA
Everything's a trap. Plot a course.

MATEO
Yes, ma'am.

BOLT
That'll cost eighty percent of the reserve.

YUSRA
Then we'd better get there the first time.

The ship shudders. Lights flicker. The viewport shows the gas giant swelling, a wall of amber fire.

SAKURA
(rising)
I'll tell the passengers the truth.

YUSRA
Doctor.

SAKURA
Captain.

YUSRA
Tell them gently.

Sakura nods and leaves. The bridge hums on. Mateo's hands move across the controls, steady now.

MATEO
Course plotted.

BOLT
Fuel line is holding. For now.

NILS
Captain, the message changed. It's in plain text now.

YUSRA
Read it.

NILS
"Marginalia, welcome. We've been waiting."

The bridge falls silent.
